  },
  "description": "KEDA as the Temporal workers' autoscaler (ADR-055): what the temporal scaler computed per worker version, what the HPA it renders actually did, the server backlog and SDK schedule-to-start it is meant to drain, and KEDA's own health. Structure follows KEDA's official config/grafana/keda-dashboard.json (v2.20.2) with a Temporal row added; every panel description names the metric and the label it depends on. exported_namespace is inherited from the official board and is VERIFY-AT-KIND. No local-stack twin: compose runs no KEDA.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [
    {
      "title": "Temporal — Workflows & Activities",
      "type": "dashboards",
      "tags": [
        "temporal"
      ],
      "asDropdown": false,
      "includeVars": false,
      "keepTime": true
    }
  ],
  "liveNow": false,
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Scaler — what KEDA computed",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Scaler metric value (backlog per worker version)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (scaledObject) (keda_scaler_metrics_value{exported_namespace=~\"$namespace\", scaledObject=~\"$scaledObject\"})",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{scaledObject}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "keda_scaler_metrics_value — the number the temporal scaler handed the HPA: this version's ApproximateBacklogCount from DescribeTaskQueue(stats). targetQueueSize is 5, so desired replicas = ceil(value / 5), floored at 1 and capped at 3. Label note: KEDA stamps its own `namespace` label (the ScaledObject's namespace), so under a Prometheus-operator scrape the target's namespace wins and KEDA's becomes `exported_namespace` — the label the official KEDA board uses and the one this board follows. If the Kind audit shows the series carrying `namespace` instead, change the variable query and this filter in one commit (VERIFY-AT-KIND)."
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Desired vs target (value ÷ targetQueueSize 5)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (scaledObject) (keda_scaler_metrics_value{exported_namespace=~\"$namespace\", scaledObject=~\"$scaledObject\"}) / 5",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{scaledObject}} desired"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (horizontalpodautoscaler) (kube_horizontalpodautoscaler_status_current_replicas{namespace=~\"$namespace\", horizontalpodautoscaler=~\"keda-hpa-.*\"})",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "B",
          "legendFormat": "{{horizontalpodautoscaler}} current"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The scaler's raw desired count against what the HPA actually set. A persistent gap in the same direction is the HPA's stabilization window or the min/max clamp, not a fault. HPA names are keda-hpa-<ScaledObject name>; the ScaledObject name is the controller's hashed per-version name, so match by regex."
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "id": 4,
      "type": "state-timeline",
      "title": "Scaler active",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "custom": {
            "fillOpacity": 70,
            "lineWidth": 0
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "transparent",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "idle",
                  "color": "transparent"
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "active",
                  "color": "green"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "showValue": "never",
        "rowHeight": 0.8,
        "mergeValues": true,
        "alignValue": "left",
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": false
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "single",
          "sort": "none"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "max by (scaledObject) (keda_scaler_active{exported_namespace=~\"$namespace\", scaledObject=~\"$scaledObject\"})",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{scaledObject}}"
        }
      ],
      "description": "keda_scaler_active — 1 while the backlog is above activationTargetQueueSize (0 here, so any backlog). A version that is active for minutes while replicas do not move is the shape TemporalTaskQueueBacklogGrowing pages on."
    },
